      {
        "at": 0.3,
        "text": "Try solving this in thirty seconds."
      },
      {
        "at": 2.4,
        "text": "The area of right triangle A B C is sixty. What's its perimeter?"
      },
      {
        "at": 6.2,
        "text": "Here's the triangle. One leg is fifteen."
      },
      {
        "at": 9.2,
        "text": "Pause, and drop your answer in the comments."
      },
      {
        "at": 12.2,
        "text": "Area is half of base times height. So half of fifteen, times A C, is sixty. That makes A C eight."
      },
      {
        "at": 18.55,
        "text": "Now Pythagoras. Eight squared plus fifteen squared is two eighty-nine. So A B is seventeen."
      },
      {
        "at": 24.5,
        "text": "Add all three sides. Eight, plus fifteen, plus seventeen, is forty."
      },
      {
        "at": 28.85,
        "text": "So the answer is D."
      },
      {
